1
00:00:01,960 --> 00:00:03,480
好了 我出门了
Okay. I'm taking off.

2
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:04,480
你要去哪
Where are you going?

3
00:00:05,020 --> 00:00:05,980
我们不是约好要让那只鸡度过
I thought we were going to give a chicken

4
00:00:05,980 --> 00:00:07,060
生命中最美好的一天吗
the best day of its life.

5
00:00:07,260 --> 00:00:09,160
我也不想总是改时间
I hate that we keep rescheduling that,

6
00:00:09,180 --> 00:00:12,120
可是当地产经纪人就得周末上班
but being a realtor man means working on sundays,

7
00:00:12,132 --> 00:00:14,400
就像神父和莱斯利·斯塔尔一样
like priests and Lesley Stahl.

8
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:15,700
祝你好运 亲爱的
Good luck out there, honey.

9
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:16,900
我们都指着你了
We're all counting on you.

10
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:18,420
希望能成功到达那里
Just got to make it through this commute.

11
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:20,580
到了会告诉你的
I'll call when I get there.

12
00:00:23,540 --> 00:00:24,420
我到了
I'm there!

13
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:26,500
祝你愉快
Have a great day!

14
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:29,980
我在帮我们的邻居杰瑞卖房子
I am handling the sale of our neighbor Jerry's house.

15
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:32,100
他要卖了房子搬去单身公寓
He's selling it and moving into a bachelor pad

16
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:33,680
因为他已经正式离婚了
now that he's officially divorced.

17
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:35,000
这太棒了
Which is great!

18
00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:36,180
我没觉得很棒
Well, I don't know about "great."

19
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:39,200
可能的确来去自由一些
I mean, you can come and go as you please, I suppose,

20
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:41,420
也许还能和送快递的姑娘调调情
and maybe see what's up with the U.P.S. girl

21
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:42,920
她总是会问你是否健身
who's always asking if you work out, or --

22
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:46,020
这很棒是因为我们居然有机会
It's great because we have the rare opportunity

23
00:00:46,020 --> 00:00:47,220
选择我们的新邻居
to choose our new neighbors.

24
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:48,460
当然同时还要
While still looking out

25
00:00:48,460 --> 00:00:50,565
兼顾我客户的利益
for my client's best interests, of course.

26
00:00:50,565 --> 00:00:52,032
你懂的
Winkwink.

27
00:00:52,206 --> 00:00:53,500
我现在处境有点微妙
I'm in kind of in a delicate spot --

28
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:55,480
夹在老婆和隔壁的哥们之间左右为难
stuck between my wife and the guy next door,

29
00:00:55,480 --> 00:00:58,620
不过我有把握同时满足他们两个
but I'm pretty sure I can satisfy them both simultaneously.

30
00:01:00,220 --> 00:01:01,600
好了 他们来了 他们来了
Okay. That's them. That's them.

31
00:01:01,840 --> 00:01:02,680
所有人都装成做园艺的样子
Everybody look like you're gardening.

32
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:04,340
卢克 拿起那把小锄头
Luke, grab that little hoe.

33
00:01:04,750 --> 00:01:07,111
她说的不是那个意思
Uh, I -- I don't think that's what she meant.

34
00:01:07,220 --> 00:01:07,820
对吧
Is it?

35
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:09,520
我们为什么要这么做
Okay, why are we doing this?

36
00:01:09,620 --> 00:01:11,880
这是他们第三次来了 我们要表现好点
This is their third visit, and we want to look good.

37
00:01:12,980 --> 00:01:14,220
他们有什么好的
What's so great about them?

38
00:01:14,220 --> 00:01:16,000
他们在原来的社区很受欢迎
They're very well-liked in their neighborhood,

39
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:17,360
他们的孩子很懂礼貌
they have very polite children,

40
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:18,780
他们很有深度
and they are sophisticated.

41
00:01:19,060 --> 00:01:21,160
那个男的收藏了很多红酒
The husband is a huge wine collector.

42
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:22,160
这才是重点
Oh, there it is.

43
00:01:22,460 --> 00:01:23,840
好了 快点 快点
All right, this is it. This is it.

44
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:24,819
看着精神点儿
Okay, look sharp.

45
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:26,380
卢克 你脸上是什么
Luke, what's on your face?

46
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:27,860
我不知道 什么颜色的
I don't know. What color is it?

47
00:01:27,860 --> 00:01:29,320
怎么弄不下来
Why isn't it coming off?

48
00:01:30,460 --> 00:01:32,360
这种行为太奇怪了
This feels like a panic move.

49
00:01:32,740 --> 00:01:34,920
你们好
Hey... again. Hello.

50
00:01:35,035 --> 00:01:36,760
-早安 -你们好
- Morning. - Hello.

51
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:38,100
家庭园艺时间
Just doing a little family gardening.

52
00:01:41,260 --> 00:01:42,220
回见
See ya.

53
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:43,760
顺便说一句那是花生酱
It's peanut butter, by the way.

54
00:01:44,340 --> 00:01:46,180
可两天前花生酱就吃光了
We ran out of peanut butter two days ago.

55
00:02:01,380 --> 00:02:03,160
我的神哪 管用了
Holy cow. It works!

56
00:02:03,820 --> 00:02:04,580
他在干嘛
What is he doing?

57
00:02:05,260 --> 00:02:08,100
他把袜子放进汽水包装里再拿出来
He's putting socks in a soda box and pulling them out.

58
00:02:08,420 --> 00:02:09,040
不
Oh, no.

59
00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:11,080
这和我祖母那时开始
This is like when my grandmother

60
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:13,340
用仙人掌梳头发一样
started combing her hair with a cactus.

61
00:02:14,201 --> 00:02:17,280
杰 杰 总统是谁
Jay, Jay, who is the president?

62
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:18,880
这玩意儿能让我当上总统
I will be when they see this.

63
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:20,080
瞧瞧这个
Check this out.

64
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:22,100
我在卧室里最大的难题是什么
What's my biggest problem in the bedroom?

65
00:02:22,808 --> 00:02:24,272
感谢上帝
Oh, thank God.

66
00:02:24,620 --> 00:02:26,940
我总是穿同一双袜子
It's that I'm always wearing the same socks

67
00:02:26,940 --> 00:02:28,540
因为它们总是在最上面
Because they're always up front.

68
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:31,960
但是这玩意能存放并轮换袜子
But this bad boy stores and rotates your socks.

69
00:02:32,220 --> 00:02:34,540
这将创造衣柜界的历史
It's gonna revolutionize the closet industry.

70
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:36,780
我真是生在一个黄金时代
What an exciting time to be alive.

71
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:38,160
我得找律师聊聊
I'm gonna get my lawyer on the horn,

72
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:39,180
早点把名字的专利申请下来
try to lock the name down.

73
00:02:39,320 --> 00:02:40,360
这个怎么样
Check this --

74
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:41,920
"袜掘机"
"Sock it to me."

75
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:44,400
"袜袜机器"怎么样
How about "Soxbox?"

76
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:44,860
歌洛莉亚 拜托
Gloria, please.

77
00:02:44,860 --> 00:02:46,480
我是要推崇一种生活方式
I'm selling a lifestyle here.

78
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:48,500
妈 我们去泳池那玩
Uh, Mom, we're gonna go head out by the pool.

79
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:50,220
不不不 等等 打个招呼
No, no, no, wait. Say hello.

80
00:02:50,220 --> 00:02:51,629
杰 这是索菲
Jay, this is Sophie.

81
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:51,980
你好
Hello.

82
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:52,760
你好 普里契特先生
Hi, Mr. Pritchett.

83
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:54,880
那是什么 自动配袜机吗
What's that? Some sort of sock dispenser?

84
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:57,220
没错 我是做衣柜生意的
Bingo! I'm in the closet business.

85
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:59,980
这是我的新发明的雏形
And this is a crude prototype of my new invention.

86
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:00,940
这创意真棒
What a great idea.

87
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:02,240
它能帮你替换袜子
You rotate your socks

88
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:03,500
这样就不会一直穿同一双了
so you don't keep wearing the same ones.

89
00:03:03,700 --> 00:03:05,040
完全正确
That's exactly right.

90
00:03:05,540 --> 00:03:06,640
我叫它"袜掘机"
I call it "Sock it to me."

91
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:07,440
这名字真妙
That's so clever.

92
00:03:07,780 --> 00:03:09,240
很幽默 还说明了它的功能
It's funny, and it tells you what it does.

93
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:10,620
想象一下用胡桃木做的样子
Imagine it in walnut.

94
00:03:10,620 --> 00:03:11,620
这怎么回事
What's happening?

95
00:03:11,620 --> 00:03:14,480
我很抱歉他这么无聊
I -- I am so sorry that he's boring you.

96
00:03:14,480 --> 00:03:15,640
不 我对这些很感兴趣
No, I like this sort of stuff.

97
00:03:15,860 --> 00:03:17,380
我爷爷厄尔也是做衣柜生意的
My grandpa Earl's in the closet business, too.

98
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:18,100
等等 厄尔
Wait, wait. Earl?

99
00:03:18,406 --> 00:03:20,060
不会是厄尔·钱伯斯吧
Not -- not Earl Chambers.

100
00:03:20,060 --> 00:03:21,980
对 他拥有"衣柜衣柜衣柜...
Yeah, he owns closets, closets, closets...

101
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:23,040
衣柜"公司 我知道
Closets. Yeah.

102
00:03:23,199 --> 00:03:24,800
我认识你爷爷
I know your grandpa.

103
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:25,840
1980年
It was 1980.

104
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:28,543
厄尔和我合办了"衣橱福尼亚"公司
Earl and I had just formed our company, Closet-Fornia.

105
00:03:28,543 --> 00:03:30,580
生意很不错 高端客户
Business was great, high-end clients,

106
00:03:30,580 --> 00:03:31,600
还有一两个名流光顾
maybe a celebrity or two.

107
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:32,920
不过我不方便说出他们的名字
I shouldn't name names. Anyway...

108
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:35,300
有一天我上班的时候
Came to work one day,

109
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:37,200
发现厄尔的桌子被清空了
and earl's desk had been cleared out.

110
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:39,840
他对我们一半的客户说了我的坏话
He had badmouthed me to half our rolodex.

111
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:40,360
我都绝望了
It was devastating.

112
00:03:41,020 --> 00:03:42,300
我只能重新开始
I had to start all over.

113
00:03:45,090 --> 00:03:45,741
算了 告诉你们吧
Well, what the hell?

114
00:03:45,741 --> 00:03:46,540
拉里·哈格曼曾是我们的客户
It was Larry Hagman.

115
00:03:46,540 --> 00:03:47,100
那家伙很棒
Heck of a guy.

116
00:03:47,100 --> 00:03:48,960
胸怀宽广似海洋
Heart as big as his hat.

117
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:51,440
这么快就回来了
Hey, you're back already?

118
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:52,740
生日派对怎么样
How was the birthday party?

119
00:03:52,860 --> 00:03:53,900
我骑了一头独角兽
I rode a unicorn.

120
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:55,460
对 没错
Yes, you did.

121
00:03:55,620 --> 00:03:56,980
自己一个人骑上去的
All by your lonesome.

122
00:03:56,980 --> 00:03:59,328
不是真的独角兽
It wasn't a real unicorn.

123
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:00,420
多谢解释
Thank you.

124
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:01,940
我准备去做作业了
I'm gonna go and do homework.

125
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:04,520
不是紧急事情别来烦我
Don't knock unless it's an actual emergency.

126
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:06,240
比如打蜘蛛什么的
Not a spider.

127
00:04:06,979 --> 00:04:08,730
普兰克老师周末还留作业吗
Ms. Plank gave her homework on the weekend?

128
00:04:08,730 --> 00:04:09,580
她才七岁
She's 7.

129
00:04:09,580 --> 00:04:11,280
我知道 那女人疯了
I know. The woman is insane.

130
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:12,180
不过听着
But listen.

131
00:04:12,521 --> 00:04:14,920
我在荧光纹身贴那里排队时听到了些消息
I heard something in the glitter-tattoo line.

132
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:15,280
什么
What?

133
00:04:15,540 --> 00:04:17,660
斯帕萝老师的班上有了一个空位
There's an opening in Miss Sparrow's class.

134
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:18,992
天哪 小卡 那太棒了
Oh, my god! Cam, that's amazing.

135
00:04:18,992 --> 00:04:19,830
我们必须把她换到那个班上
We got to get her in.

136
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:21,520
我知道 明天一早我们就去帮她换班
I know. We're going in first thing tomorrow.

137
00:04:21,880 --> 00:04:22,700
给我看看你纹了什么
Let's see it.

138
00:04:22,710 --> 00:04:24,674
两只海豚组成的红心
Two dolphins that form a heart.

139
00:04:25,295 --> 00:04:28,000
莉莉的学校有两位二年级老师
There are two second-grade teachers at Lily's school --

140
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:28,840
斯帕萝老师
Miss Sparrow,

141
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:31,680
她的课有趣而刺激
who makes learning fun and adventurous.

142
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:34,320
以及教莉莉的普兰克老师
And then there's Lily's teacher, Mrs. Plank,

143
00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:36,220
她快把莉莉逼疯了
who is stressing Lily out.

144
00:04:36,220 --> 00:04:37,420
让我们看看 宝贝
Let's see, sweetie.

145
00:04:38,300 --> 00:04:39,220
做得真棒
Good job.

146
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:42,720
不 我把蝌蚪拼错了
Oh, no! I spelled "Tadpole" wrong!

147
00:04:42,940 --> 00:04:45,580
没关系 只是个小错误而已
Oh, well, now, that's just one mistake.

148
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:47,360
普兰克老师不允许有错误
Mrs. Plank doesn't tolerate mistakes!

149
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:49,480
-好吧 -好吧
- Okay. - All right.

150
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:51,680
我称普兰克老师为"可烂老师"
I call Mrs. Plank "Mrs. Crank."

151
00:04:53,320 --> 00:04:54,120
因为
Because, you know,

152
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:55,720
我有勇气说出别人不敢说的
I have the courage to say what others won't.

153
00:04:56,460 --> 00:04:57,280
背着她说
Behind her back.

154
00:04:58,860 --> 00:05:00,780
我一年前帮上一个房主
And I also helped the previous owners

155
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:03,300
装了全新的即热式热水系统
install a brand-new tankless water heater a year ago,

156
00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:04,700
但是他们有感激我吗
but did they show any gratitude?

157
00:05:04,700 --> 00:05:05,320
没有
Nope!

158
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:07,260
因为这工作"不用谢"[谐音]
Because it's a "Tankless" job.

159
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:07,840
没错
Yes!

160
00:05:08,300 --> 00:05:09,280
搬过来吧
Please move in.

161
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:11,171
我们可以经常这么即兴创作段子
We can riff like this all the time.

162
00:05:11,560 --> 00:05:13,560
你们觉得怎么样 还喜欢吗
So, what do ya think? Do you still love it?

163
00:05:14,020 --> 00:05:14,500
当然
Absolutely.

164
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:17,460
我已经在想象在院子里种满鲜花
I can just see filling this yard with flowers.

165
00:05:17,500 --> 00:05:19,180
和我们假装在干的一样
Just like we're pretending to do.

166
00:05:20,920 --> 00:05:22,880
话说我很喜欢你的鞋子
By the way, I love those shoes.

167
00:05:23,640 --> 00:05:24,120
谢谢
Oh, thanks.

168
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:27,260
乔治的公司在为大概十家鞋子品牌做公关
George's firm does P.R. for about 10 shoe brands.

169
00:05:27,260 --> 00:05:28,260
如果我们搬进来
If we end up living here,

170
00:05:28,300 --> 00:05:29,880
相信我 你们会被淹没在鞋子的海洋
trust me, you'll be swimming in shoes.

171
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:31,740
我做过这个梦
I've had that dream.

172
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:33,900
说起梦想 你们怎么想
Speaking of dreams, what do you think?

173
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:34,980
准备好提笔签约了吗
You guys ready to pull the trigger?

174
00:05:35,740 --> 00:05:36,880
我想准备好了
I think we are.

175
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:38,487
-棒极了 -太好了
- That's great! - Yes!

176
00:05:38,487 --> 00:05:40,454
我穿六号鞋
I'm a size 6!

177
00:05:41,860 --> 00:05:43,380
自从上次我从房顶上掉下来
Not since I fell off the roof

178
00:05:43,380 --> 00:05:44,940
刚好摔在正被送来的蹦床上
while they were delivering our trampoline

179
00:05:44,940 --> 00:05:46,620
就再没发生过这么美好的事了
have things come together so beautifully.

180
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:48,020
再见
See you soon!

181
00:05:48,320 --> 00:05:48,860
成功了
We did it.

182
00:05:48,860 --> 00:05:51,860
我们就要迎来史上最棒的邻居了
We are gonna have the best neighbors ever!

183
00:05:52,420 --> 00:05:53,440
这什么声音
What's that noise?

184
00:05:54,660 --> 00:05:55,140
酷
Cool!

185
00:05:58,940 --> 00:06:00,700
我才不想看什么破房子
I don't want to see a stupid house.

186
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:04,300
你能不能闭上嘴别丢我们的脸
Hey, how 'bout you shut up and not embarrass us?

187
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:05,833
你俩能不能都闭嘴
How 'bout you both shut up?

188
00:06:05,833 --> 00:06:06,700
听你们说话都听烦了
I'm sick of listening to you.

189
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:08,460
别这么跟你爸说话
Hey, don't talk to your dad like that,

190
00:06:08,460 --> 00:06:09,800
不然就搬去跟你男友住
or you can go live with your boyfriend.

191
00:06:09,940 --> 00:06:10,980
他不是我男友
He's not my boyfriend.

192
00:06:11,300 --> 00:06:12,200
我只是跟他亲热而已
I just make out with him

193
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:13,440
这样就不用再上他的课了
so I don't have to take his class again.

194
00:06:13,660 --> 00:06:14,640
我们该去打个招呼
We should go say hi.

195
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:16,170
不 不 不 不 不 不
No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no.

196
00:06:16,180 --> 00:06:17,040
菲尔 快摘下来
Phil, shut it down.

197
00:06:17,040 --> 00:06:18,600
我在努力 这东西怎么这么结实
I'm trying! What are these things made of?

198
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:19,300
快点
Come on.

199
00:06:24,280 --> 00:06:24,680
天啊
Dude...

200
00:06:24,680 --> 00:06:26,000
我爱死这地方了
I love this place.

201
00:06:26,280 --> 00:06:26,960
我也是 亲爱的
Me too, baby.

202
00:06:26,960 --> 00:06:28,580
我一直想住在西班牙式的房子里
I always wanted a Spanish house.

203
00:06:28,580 --> 00:06:30,580
就好像住在小公牛墨西哥餐厅一样
It'll be like living at an El Torito.

204
00:06:30,580 --> 00:06:31,640
是你家人
Oh! Your family.

205
00:06:31,651 --> 00:06:34,240
你们是邻居吗 喜欢这地方吗
Hey, you the neighbors? You like living here?!

206
00:06:34,240 --> 00:06:35,260
你说什么 不好意思
What? I'm so sorry.

207
00:06:35,320 --> 00:06:38,100
交通噪音太大 我听不清
It's so hard to hear over all that freeway noise, right?

208
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:39,720
这样就不会有人抱怨
Hey, then no one's gonna complain

209
00:06:39,720 --> 00:06:43,180
我驾驶汽车 机车和我老婆时的噪音了
when I'm revving my cars, my bike, or my lady.

210
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:46,420
我叫罗尼·拉方丹
I'm Ronnie Lafontaine.

211
00:06:46,660 --> 00:06:50,140
这位辣妹是我老婆 安布尔
And this hot lady right here is my wife, Amber.

212
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:53,360
这两个小恶魔是塔米和小罗尼
And these two little hellraisers are Tammy and Ronnie jr.

213
00:06:53,620 --> 00:06:55,260
你好啊 辣妹
Hey, hot stuff.

214
00:06:55,260 --> 00:06:56,787
我 我 我吗
M-m-m-me?

215
00:06:57,911 --> 00:07:00,180
你好啊
Um...hello.

216
00:07:00,180 --> 00:07:02,160
这地方太好了
Damn, this neighborhood's sweet.

217
00:07:02,160 --> 00:07:03,636
离我工作的地方也很近
Yeah, it's close to my work, too.

218
00:07:03,636 --> 00:07:05,440
你是干什么工作的 罗尼
Wh-- uh, what is your line of work, Ronnie?

219
00:07:05,440 --> 00:07:07,140
我基本上算是医生
Well, I'm basically a doctor.

220
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:08,860
别谦虚了
Oh, stop being modest.

221
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:11,490
他有一大堆医用大麻药房
He owns, like, a buttload of medical-weed dispensaries.

222
00:07:11,490 --> 00:07:14,847
我就说我看你怎么这么眼... 你好
Ah, that's where I kno-- Oh, hello?

223
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:17,380
大妹子 你好像不太舒服
Honey, you look a little nauseous.

224
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:18,680
是啊 是有点
Yeah. Yeah, a little.

225
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,060
我有东西能让你舒坦些
Hey, I got something for that.

226
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:21,220
不用了
All good.

227
00:07:22,020 --> 00:07:23,720
你怎么能把她领家里来
How could you bring her to my home?

228
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:26,440
她是我的死敌的孙女
She's the granddaughter of my worst enemy.

229
00:07:26,500 --> 00:07:27,920
我又不知道是这样
I had no idea who she was.

230
00:07:27,980 --> 00:07:29,460
我是在戏剧小组认识她的
I met her in my theater group.

231
00:07:29,471 --> 00:07:32,020
我演凯撒 她演3号小妾
I'm Caesar, and she's Concubine #3.

232
00:07:32,020 --> 00:07:32,820
缘由天定躲不掉
It was bound to happen.

233
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:35,400
厄尔·钱伯斯是个在背后暗算人的骗子
Earl Chambers is a liar and a backstabber

234
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:37,960
他背叛了我却从未道歉
who betrayed me and never apologized.

235
00:07:38,660 --> 00:07:40,340
杰 拜托 不就是衣柜吗
Jay, please. It's just closets.

236
00:07:40,380 --> 00:07:41,620
我倒希望是"就是衣柜"公司的人
I wish it was just closets.

237
00:07:41,660 --> 00:07:42,780
那帮人还值得我尊敬
I respect those guys.

238
00:07:43,041 --> 00:07:45,200
糟了 她看到我的"袜掘机"了
Damn it, she saw the Sock It To Me!

239
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:45,880
那又怎样
So what?

240
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:47,800
如果她能记得它的工作原理
If she can remember how it works,

241
00:07:47,860 --> 00:07:49,700
她会一五一十地告诉厄尔的
She's gonna tell Earl all about it.

242
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:51,300
她会记得它的工作原理
If she can remember how it works?

243
00:07:51,300 --> 00:07:53,040
不就是把袜子放到盒子里
You put the sock in a box.

244
00:07:53,040 --> 00:07:54,600
连乔都能想得出来
Even Joe could have thought of that.

245
00:07:55,960 --> 00:07:57,960
你还跟她说过什么
What else did you discuss with her?

246
00:07:57,960 --> 00:07:59,060
你提到过
Did you mention

247
00:07:59,060 --> 00:08:02,080
我们在实验发光晾衣杆的事吗
we've been experimenting with lighted hanging rods?

248
00:08:02,360 --> 00:08:03,800
我不太擅长和女生聊天
I don't have a great rap with girls,

249
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:04,800
可我不会傻到聊那个
but it's better than that.

250
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:06,080
那你只能和别人聊了
Well, you're gonna use it with someone else

251
00:08:06,080 --> 00:08:07,520
因为我禁止你再见她
'cause I forbid you to see her.

252
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:09,120
-什么 -这不公平
- What? - That's not fair.

253
00:08:09,240 --> 00:08:11,460
不公平的是在我重拾生活的同时
What's not fair is me picking up the pieces of my life

254
00:08:11,460 --> 00:08:14,416
厄尔却可以出演《豪门恩怨》
while Earl gets to be an extra on "Dallas"!

255
00:08:21,633 --> 00:08:22,880
邓菲
Hey, Dunphy.

256
00:08:24,520 --> 00:08:26,060
我在打量这棵树
Just checking out this tree.

257
00:08:26,680 --> 00:08:27,640
是啊
Oh, yeah,

258
00:08:28,460 --> 00:08:29,760
乱透了 是吧
it's really messy, right?

259
00:08:29,760 --> 00:08:31,180
把房子的光都挡住了
And it makes the house so dark.

260
00:08:31,180 --> 00:08:34,440
不过那些老鼠挺喜欢的
But the -- the rats love it, so...

261
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:36,380
别担心 我会把它砍掉的
Yeah, no worries. I'm gonna cut it down.

262
00:08:36,620 --> 00:08:39,300
我可不想让树液滴到我的躺椅上
I don't want all this sap all over my lawn couch.

263
00:08:40,040 --> 00:08:42,360
我要是你就不会先急着砍树 罗尼
Well, I wouldn't fire up your chainsaw just yet, Ronnie.

264
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:43,600
房地产市场竞争很激烈
It's a very competitive market.

265
00:08:43,740 --> 00:08:44,620
还有别的买家吗
Is there another buyer?

266
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:46,220
我不能告诉你
I really shouldn't say.

267
00:08:46,865 --> 00:08:49,880
你这是 在玩地产经纪人的花招吗
Is this -- is this one of those realtor tricks?

268
00:08:49,880 --> 00:08:50,240
不是
No.

269
00:08:50,340 --> 00:08:52,360
你是想用这种方法让我提价吗
Where you're trying to get me to raise my offer?

270
00:08:52,420 --> 00:08:52,960
不是
Oh, no.

271
00:08:52,980 --> 00:08:53,640
很可惜它奏效了
Well, it's working.

272
00:08:53,640 --> 00:08:56,220
这样吧 我再加五万
All right. I'll throw in another 50 grand.

273
00:08:56,700 --> 00:08:58,400
什么 这主意糟透了
What?! That's a terrible idea!

274
00:08:58,840 --> 00:09:00,060
我不能错过这房子
I'm not losing the house.

275
00:09:00,100 --> 00:09:01,980
我在里面干了人生最爽的一炮
I had the best sex of my life in there.

276
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:02,600
什么时候干的
When?!

277
00:09:06,289 --> 00:09:07,637
打扰了 可烂老师
Excuse me, Ms. Crank.

278
00:09:07,637 --> 00:09:08,940
普兰克 普兰克老师
-Plank. Ms. Plank?

279
00:09:08,940 --> 00:09:09,340
什么事
Yes?

280
00:09:09,340 --> 00:09:12,360
你好 是个哭脸印章啊
Hi. I-- Oh. A frowny-face stamp.

281
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:13,280
我都不知道还有这玩意
I didn't know they made those.

282
00:09:13,400 --> 00:09:15,000
我是从德国特别订做的
I had to special order it from Germany.

283
00:09:15,180 --> 00:09:15,880
你们有什么事
May I help you?

284
00:09:15,892 --> 00:09:17,640
我们是莉莉的家长
Uh, well, we're Lily's parents.

285
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:18,360
有什么问题吗
Is there a problem?

286
00:09:18,560 --> 00:09:19,940
也算不上是问题
Not so much a problem, no.

287
00:09:19,940 --> 00:09:22,300
是啊 更像是给您一个机会...
No, more of an opportunity for you to...

288
00:09:22,300 --> 00:09:23,420
减轻工作负担
lighten your workload.

289
00:09:23,420 --> 00:09:27,061
也许能让哭脸印章倒过来
Maybe turn that frowny-face stamp upside down.

290
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:28,120
让我猜猜
Let me guess--

291
00:09:28,300 --> 00:09:29,060
你们听说了
you've heard there's

292
00:09:29,069 --> 00:09:31,340
年轻的斯帕萝老师的班上有空位了
an opening in young Ms. Sparrow's classroom.

293
00:09:31,340 --> 00:09:32,380
-什么 -哪个老师
- What? - Miss who?

294
00:09:32,380 --> 00:09:33,678
-是那个 你确定 -有空缺
- Is this-- Do you-- - An opening?

295
00:09:33,820 --> 00:09:34,160
没听说
No.

296
00:09:34,580 --> 00:09:35,820
不好意思
Oh, I'm sorry.

297
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:37,760
请原谅我妄下结论
Forgive me for jumping to conclusions.

298
00:09:38,260 --> 00:09:40,480
请你们告诉我你们有何贵干
By all means, tell me why you're here.

299
00:09:41,594 --> 00:09:43,718
我们 我们就是顺路
Well, we-- we've just, uh, stopped by,

300
00:09:43,718 --> 00:09:44,729
过来一趟
Uh, in the neighborhood to

301
00:09:44,740 --> 00:09:46,520
-打个招呼 -问个好 你好
- say hello. - Say hi. Hi.

302
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:48,820
另外...
And, also, um...

303
00:09:49,640 --> 00:09:51,260
有关您推荐给莉莉的
about this opening in Miss Sparrow's class

304
00:09:51,260 --> 00:09:52,640
斯帕萝老师的班
that you suggested for Lily.

305
00:09:52,640 --> 00:09:54,540
您觉得这事...
Is that something that you would...

306
00:09:54,540 --> 00:09:56,480
您觉得这主意好吗
That you would think would be a good idea?

307
00:09:56,600 --> 00:09:57,760
家长无权
Parents are not allowed

308
00:09:57,760 --> 00:09:59,240
给孩子选择老师
to choose their children's teachers.

309
00:09:59,380 --> 00:10:00,040
当然了
No, and, of course,

310
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:02,720
我肯定不会为莉莉要求特殊对待
I would never suggest special treatment for Lily

311
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:05,720
尽管她曾是孤儿 又是外国移民
even if she is a -- a former orphan and minority

312
00:10:05,732 --> 00:10:07,872
还是两个同志的女儿
and-- and daughter of two gay men.

313
00:10:07,872 --> 00:10:09,860
对她来说可是一大负担
That's a big load on those little shoulders.

314
00:10:09,860 --> 00:10:12,780
你们的意思是你们女儿处于不利
Are you suggesting that your daughter is at a disadvantage

315
00:10:12,780 --> 00:10:15,040
因为她是被同志家庭养大的吗
because she's being raised by gay parents?

316
00:10:15,860 --> 00:10:17,020
这能打动您吗
Is it working?

317
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:23,000
好吧 说实话
Okay. You know what?

318
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:26,141
我们只不过觉得莉莉不太接受
Look. Uh, we just don't think that Lily responds

319
00:10:26,141 --> 00:10:28,320
您的教学方法
to your, uh, teaching methods,

320
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:31,900
我们觉得她在斯帕萝老师的课上会更开心
and we think she would be happier in Miss Sparrow's class.

321
00:10:32,580 --> 00:10:34,220
在那个被她
We would all be happier

322
00:10:34,220 --> 00:10:37,880
称为教室的游乐场里我们都会更开心的
in that new-age drum circle she calls a classroom.

323
00:10:37,880 --> 00:10:39,460
好吧 我们无意冒犯
Okay, well, we didn't mean to offend you.

324
00:10:39,500 --> 00:10:41,280
我们不是说你比她的差
We're not saying you're any worse than her.

325
00:10:41,640 --> 00:10:42,100
比她差
She.

326
00:10:42,100 --> 00:10:42,647
您说什么
Ma'am?

327
00:10:42,647 --> 00:10:44,038
比她差
"Than she."

328
00:10:44,380 --> 00:10:45,780
这才是正确的语法
That's proper English.

329
00:10:46,140 --> 00:10:47,660
真遗憾莉莉学不到了
It's too bad Lily won't learn it.

330
00:10:48,220 --> 00:10:49,360
所以她能去咯
So she can go.

331
00:10:49,460 --> 00:10:51,380
据我所知 她已经去了
As far as I'm concerned, she's gone already.

332
00:10:51,940 --> 00:10:53,860
又一个落在后面的小孩
One more child left behind.

333
00:10:54,160 --> 00:10:55,900
知道吗 不 莉莉会很好的
Okay, you know what? No. Lily will be fine,

334
00:10:55,900 --> 00:10:57,780
因为她会在一个更有爱的环境里
'cause she's gonna have the chance to thrive

335
00:10:57,780 --> 00:10:59,360
有蓬勃发展的机会
in a more supportive environment.

336
00:10:59,580 --> 00:11:01,420
是啊 你没必要担心她
Yeah, you don't need to worry about she.

337
00:11:04,440 --> 00:11:06,720
来这里真是个好主意 歌洛莉亚
This place is a great idea, Gloria.

338
00:11:06,740 --> 00:11:07,380
我跟你说过吗
Did I ever tell you

339
00:11:07,380 --> 00:11:09,100
我就是在这里第一次吃了椒盐卷饼面包
this is where I first tried pretzel bread?

340
00:11:09,258 --> 00:11:10,990
你好 杰
Hello, Jay.

341
00:11:11,620 --> 00:11:12,500
你好 厄尔
Hello, Earl.

342
00:11:13,100 --> 00:11:14,480
我邀请了他
I invited him

343
00:11:14,480 --> 00:11:17,180
好让你们能放下彼此间过去的矛盾
so that you two finally can bury the machete.

344
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:19,740
这个人渣曾在背后给过我一"矛"
Well, this scumbag already buried it in my back.

345
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:20,960
你个王八蛋
You son of a bitch!

346
00:11:21,060 --> 00:11:22,540
别这样 别这样
No! No! No! No!

347
00:11:22,960 --> 00:11:24,360
住手 坐下来
Stop it! Sit down!

348
00:11:24,940 --> 00:11:26,160
这太疯狂了
This is crazy.

349
00:11:26,540 --> 00:11:27,820
你俩得成为朋友
You two need to be friends.

350
00:11:28,040 --> 00:11:29,600
世界上只有你们两个人
You're the only two people in the world

351
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:31,080
这么在意衣柜
that care so much about closets.

352
00:11:31,180 --> 00:11:32,040
这太愚蠢了
This is silly!

353
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:33,720
那些摆放着
I guess those angled shelves

354
00:11:33,720 --> 00:11:35,980
你的宝贝鞋子的架子才愚蠢
that display all your precious shoes are silly.

355
00:11:36,100 --> 00:11:37,620
或者旋转领带架子
Or the rotating tie rack

356
00:11:37,620 --> 00:11:40,140
那能帮脑外科医生节约珍贵的时间
that helps a brain surgeon save valuable seconds,

357
00:11:40,140 --> 00:11:41,220
也许救下一条人命
and, just maybe, a life.

358
00:11:41,220 --> 00:11:42,500
你当时对我步步阻挠
You fought me every step of the way on that.

359
00:11:42,500 --> 00:11:44,280
因为科技还没发展到那种地步
Because the technology wasn't there yet.

360
00:11:44,280 --> 00:11:45,282
人们会受伤的
People were gonna get hurt!

361
00:11:45,282 --> 00:11:47,009
-如果你能听听 -够了
- If you would open your ears -- - Enough!

362
00:11:48,040 --> 00:11:49,840
你俩表现得像小孩子一样
You two are acting like two little boys.

363
00:11:49,978 --> 00:11:51,980
所以我要用我妈妈对付
So I'm gonna have to handle this

364
00:11:51,980 --> 00:11:53,960
我的两个弟弟的方法来对你们
how my mother handled my two brothers.

365
00:11:54,500 --> 00:11:56,900
你俩要么解决这事
It's either you two work this out...

366
00:11:56,900 --> 00:12:00,320
要么杀了对方
...or you kill each other.

367
00:12:04,360 --> 00:12:07,020
当疯狂的大麻毒贩提高报价时
When Reefer Madness raised his offer,

368
00:12:07,020 --> 00:12:08,140
我们邀请了汤普森夫妇过来
we invited the Thompsons over

369
00:12:08,140 --> 00:12:10,340
试图说服他们也提高报价
to try to convince them to raise theirs.

370
00:12:10,340 --> 00:12:11,300
我们想向他们展示
We wanted to show them

371
00:12:11,300 --> 00:12:12,680
那所房子的最大优点
that the best thing about that house

372
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:14,340
就是它的位置
is its location.

373
00:12:14,340 --> 00:12:16,529
它位于邓菲家旁边
It's Dunphy-adjacent.

374
00:12:17,120 --> 00:12:19,000
今晚过得很开心
That was so much fun.

375
00:12:19,180 --> 00:12:20,300
你们很快会给我们答复吧
We'll hear from you soon, huh?

376
00:12:20,840 --> 00:12:21,460
当然啦
You sure will.

377
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:22,500
比你想象的更快
Sooner than you think.

378
00:12:22,620 --> 00:12:23,940
-好吧 -再见
- All right. - Okay, bye.

379
00:12:23,940 --> 00:12:25,952
-小心开车 -回头见
- Drive safe. - See ya.

380
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:26,940
搞定了
Nailed it.

381
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:28,420
他们走了吗
Are they gone?

382
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:29,980
是啊 但是别担心
They are, but don't you worry.

383
00:12:29,980 --> 00:12:32,360
我们很快就会经常见到他们了
We are gonna see a lot more of those two soon.

384
00:12:32,440 --> 00:12:34,280
更快收到了他们的消息
Oh, and hearing from them even sooner.

385
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:37,217
看来某人意犹未尽啊
It looks like someone didn't get their "Phil" of Dunphy.

386
00:12:38,700 --> 00:12:39,200
不好
No.

387
00:12:39,560 --> 00:12:39,980
什么
What?

388
00:12:40,800 --> 00:12:42,260
